<h2 id="about">What this tool does</h2>
<p>UAE VAT sits at a flat 5% on most goods and services, so the arithmetic is simple — but people still trip on direction. Given a net price you add 5% to reach what the customer pays; given a shelf price that already includes VAT you have to take it back out, which is not the same as subtracting 5%. This tool does both correctly and labels each line the way a tax invoice would, so you always know whether the number in front of you is net, tax or gross.</p>
<p>Because shoppers quote VAT-inclusive totals and accountants work in exclusive amounts, the page keeps the two straight with a single mode switch. Pick whether your typed figure is a net amount or an already-inclusive one, and the calculator reverse-engineers the underlying value. The receipt-style breakdown shows Net, VAT and Gross as three tidy AED lines, exactly as you would print on a bill.</p>
<p>The standard 5% rate and AED currency load from a small config file, with the effective date and last-updated date shown on the page. Quick buttons cover the common cases — 0% for export and zero-rated supplies, 5% for standard, and a custom box for the varied rates other GCC states use — so the same tool doubles as a light multi-country VAT helper.</p>
<h2 id="how-to-use">How to use the UAE VAT Calculator <span style="color:var(--cy)">| Step by Step Guide</span></h2>
<div class="howto"><ol><li><span>Type the amount you have and pick whether it is net or already VAT-inclusive.</span></li><li><span>Choose a rate: 0% (zero-rated), 5% (UAE standard) or enter a custom rate.</span></li><li><span>Confirm the currency (AED by default) shown at the top.</span></li><li><span>Press Calculate to see the Net, VAT and Gross lines in a receipt layout.</span></li><li><span>Reset to clear the amount when moving to the next invoice.</span></li></ol></div>
<span class="ru" data-ru lang="ros">Raqam likhein aur batayein ke woh net hai ya VAT-shamil; phir rate chunein (0%, 5% ya custom). 'Calculate' dabane par Net, VAT aur Gross ki AED lines receipt jaisi ban jayengi. Rate aur currency (AED) config file se aati hai aur aap badal sakte hain.</span>
<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
<ul class="feat-list"><li>Add VAT (net → gross) and remove VAT (gross → net) directions</li><li>Correct reverse-VAT maths so subtracting 5% is not mistaken for it</li><li>Quick 0% / 5% rates plus a custom rate for other GCC countries</li><li>AED receipt-style Net / VAT / Gross breakdown</li><li>Rate, currency and effective date loaded from a config file</li><li>Recomputes live as you change the amount or rate</li></ul>
<h2 id="tips">Tips</h2>
<ul><li>A 'price including VAT' invoice is the inclusive case — pick remove, not add.</li><li>0% is for zero-rated/export supplies, not for exempt items which sit outside the VAT system.</li><li>Saudi Arabia and other GCC states differ from 5%; switch to the custom rate for those.</li><li>Round to fils only on the final line, keeping the calculator unrounded internally.</li><li>This handles a single line item — total many lines per-rate for a full return.</li></ul>
<h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
<details><summary>How do I remove VAT from a VAT-inclusive price?</summary><p>Divide the gross by (100 + rate) then multiply by the rate: on 5% that is gross × 5 ÷ 105. Taking a flat 5% off the gross is a different (and wrong) number — the calculator uses the correct formula.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is the UAE VAT rate always 5%?</summary><p>5% is the standard rate in force; a 0% rate applies to qualifying exports and zero-rated goods, and some supplies are exempt altogether. Those are not a VAT rate, so they are not the same as 0%.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I use it for other GCC countries?</summary><p>Yes — click custom and type that country's rate. Oman, Bahrain, Saudi Arabia and others have used different rates, so verify the applicable one before relying on the result.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is the uae vat calculator free to use?</summary><p>Yes — UAE VAT Calculator has no usage cap, no sign-up and no watermark, and it is not a trial: the page is a static file on https://wafasmart.tech with no billing backend behind it. </p></details>
<details><summary>Does anything get uploaded when I use uae vat calculator?</summary><p>No. UAE VAT Calculator reads your invoice amounts straight into page memory, works on it locally and hands the result back as a download — there is no upload request to intercept, store or leak, and no log of what you processed.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I use it on my phone?</summary><p>Yes. UAE VAT Calculator is mobile-first: one column, big tap targets, and the system keyboard opens with sensible number/text input. On iPhone, Files and the share sheet feed the picker the same way Downloads does on Android. The three-line receipt fits a phone screen without scrolling.</p></details>
